# Database: Not ignored for now so that it is still shared with everyone. 

# Why you might ignore it: The database file changes every time anyone runs the program and adds, 
# edits, and/or deletes data. Git isn't able to merge two people's versions of it, so if two of 
# us were to change it, one person's changes would be lost. Only remove the "#" (hashtag) at the 
# start/beginning of the last line in this file if all members of the team agree to ignore it. 

# Extra Step Needed: The database file is already uploaded (tracked) by Git, and Git keeps tracking 
# files it already tracks, even if they are ignored. So after removing the "#" (hashtag), someone/you 
# will also need to run this command once from the top folder of the repository (right click in GitHub 
# Desktop on the repository name and select "Open in Command Prompt" / "Open in PowerShell" / "Open In Terminal"):
# 
# 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 (Command) 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 🠇 
# git rm --cached "NewsAgentDeliverySystemSE/database/NewsAgentDB.db"
# 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 (Command) 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅 🠅

# "--cached" means the file is only removed from Git's records/tracking, and NOT deleted from the PC of 
# the person running the command. That person then commits and pushes.

# ----------> WARNING: <----------
# When everyone else pulls that commit, Git WILL delete their local copy of the database file.
# Everyone should back up (copy) their local NewsAgentDB.db file to a safe location somewhere outside of 
# the repository before pulling, then copy it back afterwards. 

NewsAgentDeliverySystemSE/database/*.db